saj@chinet.chi.il.us (Stephen Jacobs) writes:

>I used to think that it was impossible to choke to death on a wraith corpse,
>but I just had it happen.  My character was as full as can be, and I wouldn't
>have considered eating so much as a fortune cookie, but somehow I thought
>wraiths were safe.
SPOILER or EXPLANATION

Although a wraith doesn't add any nutrition, you still can choke over it,
as you discovered the hard way.
The problem is that there is some sort of hunger counter in NetHack.
Below 500 you get hungry, 500-1500 normal, above 1500 you are satiated
and above 2000 you choke & die (numbers may not be quite accurate, but you'll
get the idea). If you are below the satiated level (i.e. <1500) it is always
allowed to eat everything without choking & dying. For example: if you have
1499 and eat a Dragon (+1500), the counter will be 2999). If however you
are already satiated before eating this new corpse you will probably choke
(maybe the first time it will ask you to stop eating, giving you the chance
to avoid this death). Note that it is possible to eat something while being
satiated without choking as long as you stay in the 1500-2000 range.
Now eating the death wraith will add nothing, but the hunger counter is
checked again, and as you were already satiated and above the death
count (>2000) you will choke & die.
